{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1209165-is-matter-required-for-crafting-most-wonders","id":1209165,"title":"Is Matter required for crafting most Wonders?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-20T04:02:30-07:00","id":1209165,"title":"Is Matter required for crafting most Wonders?","content":"So you want to make a shirt glow, perhaps by turning thermal energy into light.<br /> <br /> Forces 3 to Transmute heat into light, Matter 2 (?) to bind it into the shirt's pattern.<br /> <br /> Now let's say you want to make it a Wonder.<br /> <br /> Forces 3 for the Transmutation and Prime 4 to make it a Wonder, invest the magickal energy into the pattern permanently.<br /> <br /> But is Matter needed here?<br /> <br /> If yes, Matter is needed for most Wonders. For fetishes (binding a spirit's pattern into an object's pattern), for grimoires (binding part of your own pattern into a book), for soulgems (binding quintessence to matter). And this would make some sense. Binding anything to a pattern should logically require the Pattern Sphere in question.<br /> <br /> BUT, this also means that Prime 4 becomes a poor investment if you don't have Matter, so I can only assume that in the case of Wonders you don't require Matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T04:14:13-07:00","id":1209167,"title":"","content":"Short answer: no.<br /> <br /> All you need in theory to make a wonder is Prime alone. The other spheres are just to make the wonder do the thing you want it to do.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need matter to lock it in to the pattern, that\u2019s what Prime does for you. You need the object in question, a great deal of quintessence, possible in the form of Tass, and the spheres required for the effect you wish to create upon the object.<br /> <br /> This whole thing of locking effects into a pattern was invented for M20, and the way they\u2019ve described it is entirely unhelpful.<br /> <br /> The way I interpret it is that locking an effect into a pattern allows it to subsist even when you are no longer in the room to run it.<br /> <br /> You can make an invisibility cloak by imbuing a cloth with Forces 2 and locking it in with Matter. This is not a true wonder and thus must be maintained by the mage as an ongoing effect, but anyone can use the cloak for its invisibility.<br /> <br /> With just Forces, you could instead just make yourself and others invisible, but without correspondence, they would have to stay near you to benefit from the effect.<br /> <br /> Using Prime to craft a wonder instead makes it permanently enchanted as an invisibility cloak, which just works without maintenance needed. Matter is not required because you are using Prime to change the fundamental aspects of the object\u2019s reality.<br /> <br /> Similarly you do not need Life to make a wonder out of something alive.<br /> <br /> If you want to make someone invisible And maintain invisibility even after the walk away from you without corr, then you\u2019d need Life to sustain the effect, but like the invisibility cloak example, you\u2019re not making them into a wonder.<br /> <br /> If you were making them into a wonder capable of turning invisible at will, then all you\u2019d need is Prime and Forces, a huge amount of quintessence, and either consent or restraint.<br /> <br /> Fetishes only require Spirit magic. If you\u2019re good at talking, then just Spirit 2 to strike a deal, otherwise Spirit 4 to stuff them in the object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 04-20-2018, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T05:20:18-07:00","id":1209190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1209165-is-matter-required-for-crafting-most-wonders?p=1209167#post1209167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short answer: no.<br /> <br /> All you need in theory to make a wonder is Prime alone. The other spheres are just to make the wonder do the thing you want it to do.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need matter to lock it in to the pattern, that\u2019s what Prime does for you. You need the object in question, a great deal of quintessence, possible in the form of Tass, and the spheres required for the effect you wish to create upon the object.<br /> <br /> This whole thing of locking effects into a pattern was invented for M20, and the way they\u2019ve described it is entirely unhelpful.<br /> <br /> The way I interpret it is that locking an effect into a pattern allows it to subsist even when you are no longer in the room to run it.<br /> <br /> You can make an invisibility cloak by imbuing a cloth with Forces 2 and locking it in with Matter. This is not a true wonder and thus must be maintained by the mage as an ongoing effect, but anyone can use the cloak for its invisibility.<br /> <br /> With just Forces, you could instead just make yourself and others invisible, but without correspondence, they would have to stay near you to benefit from the effect.<br /> <br /> Using Prime to craft a wonder instead makes it permanently enchanted as an invisibility cloak, which just works without maintenance needed. Matter is not required because you are using Prime to change the fundamental aspects of the object\u2019s reality.<br /> <br /> Similarly you do not need Life to make a wonder out of something alive.<br /> <br /> If you want to make someone invisible And maintain invisibility even after the walk away from you without corr, then you\u2019d need Life to sustain the effect, but like the invisibility cloak example, you\u2019re not making them into a wonder.<br /> <br /> If you were making them into a wonder capable of turning invisible at will, then all you\u2019d need is Prime and Forces, a huge amount of quintessence, and either consent or restraint.<br /> <br /> Fetishes only require Spirit magic. If you\u2019re good at talking, then just Spirit 2 to strike a deal, otherwise Spirit 4 to stuff them in the object.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I see. I think M20 could have more clarity there, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T13:18:27-07:00","id":1209369,"title":"","content":"Think about wonders like enchantments.<br /> Imagine you have a house and you want a security system.<br /> Prime + Corresp + Mind will be OK to have an awareness of the space<br /> A virtual adept will see the enchanted location as a bot in an IRC chan..<br /> Other people would simply &quot;feel better connected to the land/have intuition or a sixth sense&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}